mponents/schemas/IncrementalCurve\",\"INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_AVERAGE_RATE\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INCREMENTAL\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\"},\"propertyName\":\"curve_type\"},\"oneOf\":[{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/IncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/AverageRateCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\"}],\"title\":\"ValueCurve\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"energy_unit\":{\"description\":\"Energy unit for the rate denominator. Must be MMBTU or GJ when basis is FUEL_INPUT, and MWH when basis is POWER_OUTPUT.\",\"enum\":[\"MMBTU\",\"GJ\",\"MWH\"],\"title\":\"EnergyUnit\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"gwp\":{\"default\":1.0,\"description\":\"GWP100 multiplier for CO2-equivalent reporting. Must be finite and non-negative. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Dimensionless\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"mass_unit\":{\"default\":\"KG\",\"description\":\"Mass unit of the emission rate numerator\",\"enum\":[\"KG\",\"LB\",\"SHORT_TON\",\"METRIC_TON\"],\"title\":\"MassUnit\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Identifier for this emissions attribute\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"pollutant\":{\"description\":\"Pollutant identity (CO2, CO2E, CH4, N2O, NOX, SO2, PM25, PM10, HG, HAP, CUSTOM)\",\"enum\":[\"CO2\",\"CO2E\",\"CH4\",\"N2O\",\"NOX\",\"SO2\",\"CO\",\"VOC\",\"PM25\",\"PM10\",\"HG\",\"HAP\",\"CUSTOM\"],\"title\":\"PollutantType\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"start_up_adder\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Per-start emission pulse, in mass_unit. Must be finite and non-negative. Units: per mass_unit — KG: kg, LB: lb, SHORT_TON: ston, METRIC_TON: t .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"mass_unit\",\"x-units\":{\"KG\":\"kg\",\"LB\":\"lb\",\"METRIC_TON\":\"t\",\"SHORT_TON\":\"ston\"}}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"pollutant\",\"emission_rate\",\"basis\",\"energy_unit\"],\"title\":\"EmissionsData\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"EnergyReservoirStorage\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"An energy storage device, modeled as a generic energy reservoir.\\n\\nThis is suitable for modeling storage charging and discharging with average efficiency losses, ignoring the physical dynamics of the storage unit. A variety of energy storage types and chemistries can be modeled with this approach. For pumped hydro storage, alternatively see `HydroPumpTurbine` and `HydroReservoir`.\",\"properties\":{\"active_power\":{\"description\":\"Initial active power set point of the unit. For power flow, this is the steady state operating point of the system. For production cost modeling, this may or may not be used as the initial starting point for the solver, depending on the solver used. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the component is connected and online (`true`) or disconnected, offline, or down (`false`). Unavailable components are excluded during simulations.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"Base power of the unit for per unitization. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"bus\":{\"description\":\"ID of the bus that this component is connected to.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"conversion_factor\":{\"default\":1.0,\"description\":\"Conversion factor of `storage_capacity` to MWh, if different than 1.0. For example, X MWh/liter hydrogen. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Dimensionless\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"cycle_limits\":{\"default\":10000,\"description\":\"Storage Maximum number of cycles per year. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"integer\",\"x-quantity\":\"Dimensionless\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"dynamic_injector\":{\"description\":\"ID of the corresponding dynamic injection device, if any.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"efficiency\":{\"description\":\"Average efficiency [0, 1] `in` (charging/filling) and `out` (discharging/consuming) of the storage system.\",\"properties\":{\"in\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"out\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"InOut\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"energy_units\":{\"default\":\"MWH\",\"description\":\"Unit basis for `storage_capacity`. MWH is the default interchange form; MWMIN records the same energy on the minutes basis used by operational durations.\",\"enum\":[\"MWH\",\"MWMIN\"],\"title\":\"EnergyUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"initial_storage_capacity_level\":{\"description\":\"Initial storage capacity level as a ratio [0, 1.0] of `storage_capacity`. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Fraction\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"input_active_power_limits\":{\"description\":\"Minimum and maximum limits on the input active power (i.e., charging). Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"operation_cost\":{\"description\":\"Operating cost of storage. or MarketBidCost\",\"discriminator\":{\"mapping\":{\"IMPORT_EXPORT_TIME_SERIES\":\"#/components/schemas/ImportExportTimeSeriesCost\",\"MARKET_BID\":\"#/components/schemas/MarketBidCost\",\"MARKET_BID_TIME_SERIES\":\"#/components/schemas/MarketBidTimeSeriesCost\",\"STORAGE\":\"#/components/schemas/StorageCost\"},\"propertyName\":\"cost_type\"},\"oneOf\":[{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/StorageCost\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/MarketBidCost\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/MarketBidTimeSeriesCost\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/ImportExportTimeSeriesCost\"}]},\"output_active_power_limits\":{\"description\":\"Minimum and maximum limits on the output active power (i.e., discharging). Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"power_units\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis for this component's power-family fields (active/reactive/apparent power, ratings, limits, ramp rates). COMPONENT_BASE: per unit on this component's own base_power. NATURAL_UNITS: the field's physical unit.\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"prime_mover_type\":{\"description\":\"Prime mover technology according to EIA 923.\",\"enum\":[\"BA\",\"BT\",\"CA\",\"CC\",\"CE\",\"CP\",\"CS\",\"CT\",\"ES\",\"FC\",\"FW\",\"GT\",\"HA\",\"HB\",\"HK\",\"HY\",\"IC\",\"PS\",\"OT\",\"ST\",\"PVe\",\"WT\",\"WS\"],\"title\":\"PrimeMovers\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"ramp_limits\":{\"description\":\"Ramp up and ramp down limits. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW/min, COMPONENT_BASE: pu/min .\",\"properties\":{\"down\":{\"title\":\"Down\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"up\":{\"title\":\"Up\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"up\",\"down\"],\"title\":\"UpDown\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu/min\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW/min\"}},\"rating\":{\"description\":\"Maximum AC side output power rating of the unit. Not to be confused with base_power. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVA, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ApparentPower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVA\"}},\"reactive_power\":{\"description\":\"Initial reactive power set point of the unit. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"reactive_power_limits\":{\"description\":\"Minimum and maximum reactive power limits. Set to `null` if not applicable. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"self_discharge\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Self-discharge (leakage loss) as a fraction of the stored energy lost per minute (pu/min of storage_capacity), modeled as E[t] = (1 - self_discharge * dt) * E[t-1]; dt must be on the same minutes basis. Units: 1/min.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"1/min\"},\"standing_loss\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Constant standing-loss power drawn by the storage system. Reduces the effective charging power (p_in - standing_loss) and increases the power drawn from the storage when discharging (p_out + standing_loss). Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"storage_capacity\":{\"description\":\"Maximum storage capacity (can be in units of, e.g., MWh for batteries or liters for hydrogen). Divided by base_power this gives an approximate duration, assuming unity power factor: in hours under MWH, in minutes under MWMIN. Units: per energy_units — MWH: MWh, MWMIN: MWmin .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"energy_units\",\"x-units\":{\"MWH\":\"MWh\",\"MWMIN\":\"MWmin\"}},\"storage_level_limits\":{\"description\":\"Minimum and maximum allowable storage levels [0, 1], which can be used to model derates or other restrictions, such as state-of-charge restrictions on battery cycling.\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"storage_target\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Storage target at the end of simulation as ratio of storage capacity. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Fraction\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"storage_technology_type\":{\"description\":\"Storage Technology Complementary to EIA 923.\",\"enum\":[\"PTES\",\"LIB\",\"LAB\",\"FLWB\",\"SIB\",\"ZIB\",\"HGS\",\"LAES\",\"OTHER_CHEM\",\"OTHER_MECH\",\"OTHER_THERM\"],\"title\":\"StorageTech\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"available\",\"bus\",\"prime_mover_type\",\"storage_technology_type\",\"storage_capacity\",\"storage_level_limits\",\"initial_storage_capacity_level\",\"rating\",\"active_power\",\"input_active_power_limits\",\"output_active_power_limits\",\"efficiency\",\"reactive_power\",\"base_power\",\"power_units\",\"operation_cost\"],\"title\":\"EnergyReservoirStorage\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"ExponentialLoad\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"A voltage-dependent ZIP load, most commonly used for dynamics modeling.\\n\\nAn `ExponentialLoad` models active power as P = P0 * V^α and reactive power as Q = Q0 * V^β, where the exponents α and β select govern the voltage dependency. For an alternative three-part formulation of the ZIP model, see `StandardLoad`. For a simpler load model with no voltage dependency, see `PowerLoad`.\",\"properties\":{\"active_power\":{\"description\":\"Active power coefficient, P0. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"alpha\":{\"description\":\"Exponent relating voltage dependency for active power. 0 = constant power only, 1 = constant current only, and 2 = constant impedance only.\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the component is connected and online (`true`) or disconnected, offline, or down (`false`). Unavailable components are excluded during simulations.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"Base power of the unit for per unitization. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"beta\":{\"description\":\"Exponent relating voltage dependency for reactive power. 0 = constant power only, 1 = constant current only, and 2 = constant impedance only.\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"bus\":{\"description\":\"ID of the bus that this component is connected to.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"conformity\":{\"default\":\"UNDEFINED\",\"description\":\"Indicates whether the specified load is conforming or non-conforming.\",\"enum\":[\"NON_CONFORMING\",\"CONFORMING\",\"UNDEFINED\"],\"title\":\"LoadConformity\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"dynamic_injector\":{\"description\":\"ID of the corresponding dynamic injection device, if any.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_active_power\":{\"description\":\"Maximum active power that this load can demand. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"max_reactive_power\":{\"description\":\"Maximum reactive power that this load can demand. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"power_units\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis for this component's power-family fields (active/reactive/apparent power, ratings, limits, ramp rates). COMPONENT_BASE: per unit on this component's own base_power. NATURAL_UNITS: the field's physical unit.\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"reactive_power\":{\"description\":\"Reactive power coefficient, Q0. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"available\",\"bus\",\"active_power\",\"reactive_power\",\"alpha\",\"beta\",\"base_power\",\"power_units\",\"max_active_power\",\"max_reactive_power\"],\"title\":\"ExponentialLoad\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"FACTSControlDevice\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"Facts control devices.\\n\\nMost often used in AC power flow studies as a control of voltage and, active and reactive power.\",\"properties\":{\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the component is connected and online (`true`) or disconnected, offline, or down (`false`). Unavailable components are excluded during simulations.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"System base power for per-unitization of this component's per-unit fields, recorded per component in lieu of a system-level table. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"bus\":{\"description\":\"Sending end bus number.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"control_mode\":{\"description\":\"Control mode. Used to describe the behavior of the control device. in psy5 a required param with an option to be nothing\",\"enum\":[\"OOS\",\"NML\",\"BYP\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"dynamic_injector\":{\"description\":\"ID of the corresponding dynamic injection model for FACTS control device, if any.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_reactive_power\":{\"default\":9999.0,\"description\":\"Independent maximum reactive power ceiling; the device reactive limit is min(the current/susceptance law on max_shunt_current, this value). Non-binding at the 9999.0 default. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"max_shunt_current\":{\"description\":\"Maximum shunt current at the sending end bus; entered at unity voltage. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVA, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ApparentPower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVA\"}},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"power_units\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis for this component's power-family fields (active/reactive/apparent power, ratings, limits, ramp rates). COMPONENT_BASE: per unit on this component's own base_power. NATURAL_UNITS: the field's physical unit.\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"reactive_power_required\":{\"description\":\"Total reactive power required to hold voltage at sending bus, as a fraction in the range 0-1. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Fraction\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"regulated_bus_number\":{\"default\":0,\"description\":\"Bus whose voltage this device regulates; 0 means local (sending) bus (PSS/E FCREG). Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"integer\",\"x-quantity\":\"Dimensionless\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"shunt_control_type\":{\"default\":\"STATCOM\",\"description\":\"Device class selecting the reactive-limit law (SVC vs STATCOM).\",\"enum\":[\"SVC\",\"STATCOM\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"voltage_setpoint\":{\"description\":\"Voltage setpoint at the sending end bus in kV, it has to be a `PV` bus. Units: kV. Units: per voltage_setpoint_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Voltage\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"voltage_setpoint_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"kV\"}},\"voltage_setpoint_units\":{\"default\":\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"description\":\"Unit basis for voltage_setpoint. COMPONENT_BASE (pu on the bus base voltage) is PSS/E RAW native (VSET).\",\"enum\":[\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"COMPONENT_BASE\"],\"title\":\"VoltageUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"name\",\"id\",\"available\",\"bus\",\"max_shunt_current\",\"reactive_power_required\",\"voltage_setpoint\",\"base_power\",\"power_units\"],\"title\":\"FACTSControlDevice\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"FixedAdmittance\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"A fixed admittance.\\n\\nMost often used in dynamics or AC power flow studies as a source of reactive power.\",\"properties\":{\"Y\":{\"description\":\"Fixed admittance. Units: per admittance_units — NATURAL_UNITS: S, COMPONENT_MVAR: MVAr .\",\"properties\":{\"imag\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"real\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"ComplexNumber\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"Susceptance\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"admittance_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_MVAR\":\"MVAr\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"S\"}},\"admittance_units\":{\"default\":\"COMPONENT_MVAR\",\"description\":\"Unit basis for the shunt admittance Y. COMPONENT_MVAR is PSS/E RAW native (Mvar/MW at unity voltage).\",\"enum\":[\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"COMPONENT_MVAR\"],\"title\":\"ShuntAdmittanceUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the component is connected and online (`true`) or disconnected, offline, or down (`false`). Unavailable components are excluded during simulations.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"System base power for per-unitization of this component's per-unit fields, recorded per component in lieu of a system-level table. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"bus\":{\"description\":\"ID of the bus that this component is connected to.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"dynamic_injector\":{\"description\":\"ID of the corresponding dynamic injection model for admittance, if any.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"available\",\"bus\",\"Y\",\"base_power\"],\"title\":\"FixedAdmittance\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"FixedForcedOutage\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"Supplemental attribute recording a component's forced outage status directly, rather than as a probability. `outage_status` is 1 when the component is outaged and 0 when it is available, and it can be backed by a time series drawn from a stochastic simulation or from historical records.\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"monitored_components\":{\"default\":[],\"description\":\"IDs of devices whose post-contingency state should be modeled when this outage occurs. Empty by default; semantics of an empty list are decided by the downstream consumer.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"outage_status\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"outage_status\"],\"title\":\"FixedForcedOutage\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"FuelCurve\":{\"description\":\"Variable operation cost of a device expressed in fuel consumed — MBTU, liters, m^3 — together with the price that converts fuel to currency. Wraps a `ValueCurve` in input-output, incremental, or average-rate form; exactly one of `fuel_cost` and `fuel_cost_time_series` supplies the price.\",\"properties\":{\"fuel_cost\":{\"description\":\"Fixed fuel cost per unit of fuel, or null when fuel_cost_time_series names a time-varying one. Exactly one of the two is set; producers and consumers enforce it.\",\"type\":[\"number\",\"null\"]},\"fuel_cost_time_series\":{\"description\":\"Store-minted id of the fuel-cost time series association, or null when fuel_cost carries a fixed value. Exactly one of the two is set.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"power_units\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/UnitSystem\"},\"startup_fuel_offtake\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\",\"description\":\"Fuel consumed during startup, as a curve in the unit's fuel units.\"},\"value_curve\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/ValueCurve\"},\"variable_cost_type\":{\"const\":\"FUEL\",\"default\":\"FUEL\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"vom_cost\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\"}},\"required\":[\"value_curve\",\"power_units\",\"vom_cost\",\"variable_cost_type\"],\"title\":\"FuelCurve\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"FunctionData\":{\"description\":\"Raw mathematical data defining a function `f(x)` — coefficients or point tables with no units or interpretation attached. `function_type` selects the shape: linear, quadratic, piecewise linear through (x, y) points, or piecewise constant between x endpoints. What `x` and `y` stand for is supplied by whatever wraps this, and the `TIME_SERIES_*` variants hold a reference to a stored series in place of the numbers.\",\"discriminator\":{\"mapping\":{\"LINEAR\":\"#/components/schemas/LinearFunctionData\",\"PIECEWISE_LINEAR\":\"#/components/schemas/PiecewiseLinearData\",\"PIECEWISE_STEP\":\"#/components/schemas/PiecewiseStepData\",\"QUADRATIC\":\"#/components/schemas/QuadraticFunctionData\",\"TIME_SERIES_LINEAR\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesLinearFunctionData\",\"TIME_SERIES_PIECEWISE_LINEAR\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesPiecewiseLinearData\",\"TIME_SERIES_PIECEWISE_STEP\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesPiecewiseStepData\",\"TIME_SERIES_QUADRATIC\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesQuadraticFunctionData\"},\"propertyName\":\"function_type\"},\"oneOf\":[{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/LinearFunctionData\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/QuadraticFunctionData\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/PiecewiseLinearData\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/PiecewiseStepData\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesLinearFunctionData\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesQuadraticFunctionData\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesPiecewiseLinearData\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesPiecewiseStepData\"}],\"title\":\"FunctionData\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"GenericArcImpedance\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"A generic branch defined by a series impedance on an `Arc` between two buses.\",\"properties\":{\"active_power_flow\":{\"description\":\"Initial condition of active power flow on the line. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"arc\":{\"description\":\"An `Arc` defining this line `from` a bus `to` another bus.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the component is connected and online (`true`) or disconnected, offline, or down (`false`). Unavailable components are excluded during simulations.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"System base power for per-unitization of this component's per-unit fields, recorded per component in lieu of a system-level table. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_flow\":{\"description\":\"Maximum allowable flow on the generic impedance. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"parameter_units\":{\"default\":\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"description\":\"Unit basis for r and x. COMPONENT_BASE is per-unit on this component's base_power, which records the system base.\",\"enum\":[\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"COMPONENT_BASE\"],\"title\":\"ImpedanceUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"power_units\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis for this component's power-family fields (active/reactive/apparent power, ratings, limits, ramp rates). COMPONENT_BASE: per unit on this component's own base_power. NATURAL_UNITS: the field's physical unit.\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"r\":{\"description\":\"Resistance. Units: per parameter_units — NATURAL_UNITS: ohm, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Resistance\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"parameter_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"ohm\"}},\"reactive_power_flow\":{\"description\":\"Initial condition of reactive power flow on the line. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\