ents/schemas/CostCurve\"}},\"required\":[\"variable_operation_cost\"],\"title\":\"LoadCost\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"LoadZone\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"A load zone for electricity price analysis. The load zone can be specified when defining each `ACBus` or `DCBus` in the zone.\",\"properties\":{\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"System base power for per-unitization of this component's per-unit fields, recorded per component in lieu of a system-level table. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"peak_active_power\":{\"description\":\"Peak active power in the zone. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"peak_reactive_power\":{\"description\":\"Peak reactive power in the zone. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"power_units\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis for this component's power-family fields (active/reactive/apparent power, ratings, limits, ramp rates). COMPONENT_BASE: per unit on this component's own base_power. NATURAL_UNITS: the field's physical unit.\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"peak_active_power\",\"peak_reactive_power\",\"base_power\",\"power_units\"],\"title\":\"LoadZone\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"MarketBidCost\":{\"description\":\"Cost representation for static (non-time-varying) market bids of energy and ancillary services.\",\"properties\":{\"ancillary_service_offers\":{\"description\":\"IDs of the ancillary service components that this market bid offers into.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"cost_type\":{\"const\":\"MARKET_BID\",\"default\":\"MARKET_BID\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"curve_style\":{\"default\":0,\"description\":\"Curve-clearing style for the bid: 0 = CURVE (ordinary divisible price-setting curve, default); 1 = FIXED (clears as one indivisible all-or-nothing package over its period); 2 = VARIABLE (divisible quantity, block-priced, cannot set the settlement-point price). Corresponds to ERCOT's DAM PriceCurve curveStyle field (CURVE/FIXED/VARIABLE). A non-zero value is mutually exclusive with incremental_slope/decremental_slope.\",\"enum\":[0,1,2],\"type\":\"integer\"},\"decremental_offer_curves\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/CostCurve\",\"description\":\"Buy offer curves data as a `CostCurve` of `PiecewiseIncrementalCurve`.\"},\"decremental_slope\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Linear-interpolation flag for the decremental offer curves; false (default) is the step interpretation. Mutually exclusive with block groups on the same curve.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"incremental_offer_curves\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/CostCurve\",\"description\":\"Sell offer curves data as a `CostCurve` of `PiecewiseIncrementalCurve`.\"},\"incremental_slope\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Linear-interpolation flag for the incremental offer curves; false (default) is the step interpretation. Mutually exclusive with block groups on the same curve.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"minimum_energy_offer\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\",\"default\":{\"curve_type\":\"INPUT_OUTPUT\",\"function_data\":{\"constant_term\":0,\"function_type\":\"LINEAR\",\"proportional_term\":0}},\"description\":\"Minimum-energy offer: cost to operate at minimum stable level, in \$/MWh at the curve's minimum power, stored as submitted. \$/h sources convert at parse (MEO = no-load cost / P_min). Legacy scalar promotion: a bare scalar value `s` from a legacy source converts to an `InputOutputCurve` of `LinearFunctionData` with `constant_term = s` and `proportional_term = 0`.\"},\"shut_down\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\",\"default\":{\"curve_type\":\"INPUT_OUTPUT\",\"function_data\":{\"constant_term\":0,\"function_type\":\"LINEAR\",\"proportional_term\":0}},\"description\":\"Shut-down cost. Legacy scalar promotion: a bare scalar value `s` from a legacy source converts to an `InputOutputCurve` of `LinearFunctionData` with `constant_term = s` and `proportional_term = 0`.\"},\"start_up\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/StartUpStages\",\"description\":\"Start-up cost at different stages of the thermal cycle (hot, warm, cold).\"}},\"required\":[\"minimum_energy_offer\",\"start_up\",\"shut_down\",\"incremental_offer_curves\",\"decremental_offer_curves\",\"ancillary_service_offers\"],\"title\":\"MarketBidCost\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"MarketBidTimeSeriesCost\":{\"description\":\"Cost representation for time-varying market bids of energy and ancillary services. The static counterpart is MarketBidCost.\",\"properties\":{\"ancillary_service_offers\":{\"description\":\"IDs of the ancillary service components that this bid offers into.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"cost_type\":{\"const\":\"MARKET_BID_TIME_SERIES\",\"default\":\"MARKET_BID_TIME_SERIES\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"curve_style\":{\"default\":0,\"description\":\"Curve-clearing style for the bid: 0 = CURVE (ordinary divisible price-setting curve, default); 1 = FIXED (clears as one indivisible all-or-nothing package over its period); 2 = VARIABLE (divisible quantity, block-priced, cannot set the settlement-point price). Corresponds to ERCOT's DAM PriceCurve curveStyle field (CURVE/FIXED/VARIABLE). A non-zero value is mutually exclusive with incremental_slope/decremental_slope.\",\"enum\":[0,1,2],\"type\":\"integer\"},\"decremental_offer_curves\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/CostCurve\",\"description\":\"Buy offer curves whose value curve is a time-series-backed piecewise incremental curve. Only the TIME_SERIES_INCREMENTAL variant is admissible here; any other variant is rejected by the consuming constructor.\"},\"decremental_slope\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Linear-interpolation flag for the decremental offer curves; false (default) is the step interpretation. Mutually exclusive with block groups on the same curve.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"incremental_offer_curves\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/CostCurve\",\"description\":\"Sell offer curves whose value curve is a time-series-backed piecewise incremental curve. Only the TIME_SERIES_INCREMENTAL variant is admissible here; any other variant is rejected by the consuming constructor.\"},\"incremental_slope\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Linear-interpolation flag for the incremental offer curves; false (default) is the step interpretation. Mutually exclusive with block groups on the same curve.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"minimum_energy_offer\":{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\",\"description\":\"Minimum-energy offer: cost to operate at minimum stable level, in \$/MWh at the curve's minimum power, stored as submitted. \$/h sources convert at parse (MEO = no-load cost / P_m