x_active_power` parameter, which is instead calculated when calling `get_max_active_power()`.\",\"properties\":{\"active_power\":{\"description\":\"Initial active power set point of the unit. For power flow, this is the steady state operating point of the system. For production cost modeling, this may or may not be used as the initial starting point for the solver, depending on the solver used. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the component is connected and online (`true`) or disconnected, offline, or down (`false`). Unavailable components are excluded during simulations.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"Base power of the unit for per unitization. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"bus\":{\"description\":\"ID of the bus that this component is connected to.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"dynamic_injector\":{\"description\":\"ID of the corresponding dynamic injection device, if any.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"power_factor\":{\"description\":\"Power factor [0, 1] set-point, used in some production cost modeling and in load flow if the unit is connected to a `PQ` bus. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"PowerFactor\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"power_units\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis for this component's power-family fields (active/reactive/apparent power, ratings, limits, ramp rates). COMPONENT_BASE: per unit on this component's own base_power. NATURAL_UNITS: the field's physical unit.\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"prime_mover_type\":{\"description\":\"Prime mover technology according to EIA 923.\",\"enum\":[\"BA\",\"BT\",\"CA\",\"CC\",\"CE\",\"CP\",\"CS\",\"CT\",\"ES\",\"FC\",\"FW\",\"GT\",\"HA\",\"HB\",\"HK\",\"HY\",\"IC\",\"PS\",\"OT\",\"ST\",\"PVe\",\"WT\",\"WS\"],\"title\":\"PrimeMovers\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"rating\":{\"description\":\"Maximum AC side output power rating of the unit. Not to be confused with base_power. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVA, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ApparentPower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVA\"}},\"reactive_power\":{\"description\":\"Initial reactive power set point of the unit, used in some production cost modeling simulations. To set the reactive power in a load flow, use `power_factor`. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"available\",\"bus\",\"active_power\",\"reactive_power\",\"rating\",\"prime_mover_type\",\"power_factor\",\"base_power\",\"power_units\"],\"title\":\"RenewableNonDispatch\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"RenewablePowerPlant\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"Attribute to represent renewable power plants. Point of common coupling (PCC) connections between units are recorded as PlantAssociation rows with role='pcc'.\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the renewable power plant\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\"],\"title\":\"RenewablePowerPlant\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"ReserveDirection\":{\"description\":\"Direction a reserve product is procured in. `UP` increases generation or reduces load when demand exceeds its expected level; `DOWN` decreases generation or increases load when demand falls below it; `SYMMETRIC` procures the same quantity in both directions. Upstream this distinction is a type parameter on the reserve; here it is flattened into a property.\",\"enum\":[\"UP\",\"DOWN\",\"SYMMETRIC\"],\"title\":\"ReserveDirection\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"ServiceAssociation\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"Links a service to one component that contributes to it. One record per (service, member) pair: the many-to-many reserve-participation relation is normalized here rather than carried as a list on either side, so each membership is an individually addressable row. The type of either side is resolved through the entity registry rather than duplicated here, matching the shape of PlantAssociation and SupplementalAttributeAssociation. `entity_id` may name a Device (the reserve case), a Branch (TransmissionInterface), or another Service (GroupReserve), so no member-type discriminator is needed. The data model library stores the same relation on the device side as `Device.services`.\",\"properties\":{\"entity_id\":{\"description\":\"ID of the contributing member: a Device, a Branch, or another Service.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"service_id\":{\"description\":\"ID of the service the membership belongs to.\",\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"service_id\",\"entity_id\"],\"title\":\"ServiceAssociation\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"ShiftablePowerLoad\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"A static power load that can be partially or completed shifted to later time periods.\\n\\nThese loads are used to model demand response. This load has a target demand profile (set by a `max_active_power` time series for an operational simulation). Load in the profile can be shifted to later time periods to aid in satisfying other system needs; however, any shifted load must be served within a designated time horizon (e.g., 24 hours), which is set by `load_balance_time_horizon`.\",\"properties\":{\"active_power\":{\"description\":\"Initial steady state active power demand. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"active_power_limits\":{\"description\":\"Minimum and maximum stable active power levels. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MW\"}},\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the component is connected and online (`true`) or disconnected, offline, or down (`false`). Unavailable components are excluded during simulations.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"base_power\":{\"description\":\"Base power of the unit for per unitization. Units: MVA.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MVA\"},\"bus\":{\"description\":\"ID of the bus that this component is connected to.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"dynamic_injector\":{\"description\":\"ID of the corresponding dynamic injection device, if any.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"load_balance_time_horizon\":{\"description\":\"Number of time periods over which load must be balanced.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_active_power\":{\"description\":\"Maximum active power that this load can demand. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ActivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"