\"DC_POWER\",\"DC_VOLTAGE\",\"DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP\"],\"title\":\"VSCDCControlModes\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"dc_control_to\":{\"default\":\"DC_VOLTAGE\",\"description\":\"DC-side control mode of the `to` converter.\",\"enum\":[\"DC_POWER\",\"DC_VOLTAGE\",\"DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP\"],\"title\":\"VSCDCControlModes\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"dc_current\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"DC current on the converter flowing in the DC line, from `from` bus to `to` bus. Units: A.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"A\"},\"dc_setpoint_from\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Converter DC setpoint in the `from` bus converter. When `dc_control_from` regulates DC voltage this number is the DC voltage on the DC side of the converter; when it controls DC power this value is the power demand in MW, if positive the converter is supplying power to the AC network at the `from` bus; if negative, the converter is withdrawing power from the AC network at the `from` bus. Units: per dc_control_from — DC_POWER: MW, DC_VOLTAGE: (per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu), DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP: (per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu) .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Voltage\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"dc_control_from\",\"x-units\":{\"DC_POWER\":\"MW\",\"DC_VOLTAGE\":{\"description\":\"Units: per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"setpoint_voltage_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"kV\"}},\"DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP\":{\"description\":\"Units: per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"setpoint_voltage_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"kV\"}}}},\"dc_setpoint_to\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Converter DC setpoint in the `to` bus converter. When `dc_control_to` regulates DC voltage this number is the DC voltage on the DC side of the converter; when it controls DC power this value is the power demand in MW, if positive the converter is supplying power to the AC network at the `to` bus; if negative, the converter is withdrawing power from the AC network at the `to` bus. Units: per dc_control_to — DC_POWER: MW, DC_VOLTAGE: (per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu), DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP: (per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu) .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Voltage\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"dc_control_to\",\"x-units\":{\"DC_POWER\":\"MW\",\"DC_VOLTAGE\":{\"description\":\"Units: per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"setpoint_voltage_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"kV\"}},\"DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP\":{\"description\":\"Units: per setpoint_voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"setpoint_voltage_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"kV\"}}}},\"dc_voltage_droop_from\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"DC-voltage droop gain on the `from` converter, used when `dc_control_from` is `DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP`: `V_dc = dc_setpoint_from - dc_voltage_droop_from * P_c`. Units: pu.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Resistance\",\"x-unit\":\"pu\"},\"dc_voltage_droop_to\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"DC-voltage droop gain on the `to` converter, used when `dc_control_to` is `DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP`: `V_dc = dc_setpoint_to - dc_voltage_droop_to * P_c`. Units: pu.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Resistance\",\"x-unit\":\"pu\"},\"g\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Series conductance of the DC line. Units: per admittance_units — NATURAL_UNITS: S, COMPONENT_MVAR: MW, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Conductance\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"admittance_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"COMPONENT_MVAR\":\"MW\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"S\"}},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_dc_current_from\":{\"default\":1.0e8,\"description\":\"Maximum stable dc current limits. Units: A.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"A\"},\"max_dc_current_to\":{\"default\":1.0e8,\"description\":\"Maximum stable dc current limits. Units: A.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"A\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"power_factor_weighting_fraction_from\":{\"default\":1.0,\"description\":\"Power weighting factor fraction used in reducing the active power order and either the reactive power order when the converter rating is violated. When is 0.0, only the active power is reduced; when is 1.0, only the reactive power is reduced; otherwise, a weighted reduction of both active and reactive power is applied. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Fraction\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"power_factor_weighting_fraction_to\":{\"default\":1.0,\"description\":\"Power weighting factor fraction used in reducing the active power order and either the reactive power order when the converter rating is violated. When is 0.0, only the active power is reduced; when is 1.0, only the reactive power is reduced; otherwise, a weighted reduction of both active and reactive power is applied. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Fraction\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"power_units\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis for this component's power-family fields (active/reactive/apparent power, ratings, limits, ramp rates). COMPONENT_BASE: per unit on this component's own base_power. NATURAL_UNITS: the field's physical unit.\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"rated_ac_voltage_from\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Rated (base) AC voltage at the `from` converter's AC terminal in kV. Used as the AC voltage base for interpreting ac_setpoint_from when ac_control_from is AC_VOLTAGE; 0.0 means unspecified (the setpoint is taken as per-unit directly). Units: kV.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"kV\"},\"rated_ac_voltage_to\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Rated (base) AC voltage at the `to` converter's AC terminal in kV. Used as the AC voltage base for interpreting ac_setpoint_to when ac_control_to is AC_VOLTAGE; 0.0 means unspecified (the setpoint is taken as per-unit directly). Units: kV.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"kV\"},\"rated_dc_voltage\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Rated (base) DC voltage of the link in kV. Used as the DC voltage base for interpreting DC-voltage setpoints; 0.0 means unspecified (DC-voltage setpoints are taken as per-unit directly). Units: kV.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"kV\"},\"rating\":{\"description\":\"Maximum output power rating of the converter. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVA, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ApparentPower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVA\"}},\"rating_from\":{\"default\":1.0e8,\"description\":\"Converter rating in the `from` bus. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVA, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ApparentPower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVA\"}},\"rating_to\":{\"default\":1.0e8,\"description\":\"Converter rating in the `to` bus. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVA, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ApparentPower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVA\"}},\"reactive_power_from\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Initial condition of reactive power flowing into the from-bus. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"reactive_power_limits_from\":{\"default\":{\"max\":0.0,\"min\":0.0},\"description\":\"Limits on the Reactive Power at the `from` side. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"reactive_power_limits_to\":{\"default\":{\"max\":0.0,\"min\":0.0},\"description\":\"Limits on the Reactive Power at the `to` side. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"reactive_power_to\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Initial condition of reactive power flowing into the to-bus. Units: per power_units — NATURAL_UNITS: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"ReactivePower\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"power_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"MVAr\"}},\"remote_bus_control_from\":{\"default\":null,\"description\":\"Number of the AC bus whose voltage the `from` converter regulates when `ac_control_from` is `AC_VOLTAGE`; null regulates its own terminal bus.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"remote_bus_control_to\":{\"default\":null,\"description\":\"Number of the AC bus whose voltage the `to` converter regulates when `ac_control_to` is `AC_VOLTAGE`; null regulates its own terminal bus.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]},\"rmpct_from\":{\"default\":100.0,\"description\":\"Percent of the total Mvar required to hold the voltage at the bus regulated by the `from` converter that is contributed by this converter. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Fraction\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"rmpct_to\":{\"default\":100.0,\"description\":\"Percent of the total Mvar required to hold the voltage at the bus regulated by the `to` converter that is contributed by this converter. Units: 1.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-quantity\":\"Fraction\",\"x-unit\":\"1\"},\"setpoint_voltage_units\":{\"default\":\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"description\":\"Unit basis for the DC_VOLTAGE/DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP/AC_VOLTAGE branches of dc_setpoint_from/to and ac_setpoint_from/to. Independent of voltage_units, which covers voltage_limits_from/to only.\",\"enum\":[\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"COMPONENT_BASE\"],\"title\":\"VoltageUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"voltage_limits_from\":{\"default\":{\"max\":999.9,\"min\":0.0},\"description\":\"Limits on the Voltage at the DC `from` Bus in kV. The DC base voltage is the `dc_setpoint` of the converter with `dc_voltage_control` enabled; exactly one converter must control the DC voltage. Units: kV. Units: per voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"Voltage\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"voltage_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"kV\"}},\"voltage_limits_to\":{\"default\":{\"max\":999.9,\"min\":0.0},\"description\":\"Limits on the Voltage at the DC `to` Bus in kV. The DC base voltage is the `dc_setpoint` of the converter with `dc_voltage_control` enabled; exactly one converter must control the DC voltage. Units: kV. Units: per voltage_units — NATURAL_UNITS: kV, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"max\":{\"title\":\"Max\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"min\":{\"title\":\"Min\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"MinMax\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"Voltage\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"voltage_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"kV\"}},\"voltage_units\":{\"default\":\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"description\":\"Unit basis for the DC bus voltage limits (voltage_limits_from/to only). Independent of setpoint_voltage_units, which covers dc_setpoint_from/to and ac_setpoint_from/to.\",\"enum\":[\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"COMPONENT_BASE\"],\"title\":\"VoltageUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"available\",\"arc\",\"active_power_flow\",\"rating\",\"active_power_limits_from\",\"active_power_limits_to\",\"base_power\",\"power_units\"],\"title\":\"TwoTerminalVSCLine\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"TwoWindingTransformer\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"A two-winding transformer connecting two buses.\\n\\nAll series electrical data — the modeled arc, tap, phase shift, series impedance `r`/`x`, ratings, per-winding base power, base voltages, and control — lives on the single `TransformerCircuit` referenced by `circuit`; availability is circuit-level. The `magnetizing_shunt` admittance and its `shunt_location` are transformer-level. The model uses an equivalent circuit assuming the impedance is on the high-voltage side and allocates iron losses and magnetizing susceptance according to `shunt_location`. The transformer's device base is the circuit's `base_power`.\",\"properties\":{\"admittance_units\":{\"default\":\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"description\":\"Unit basis for the magnetizing_shunt admittance.\",\"enum\":[\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"COMPONENT_MVAR\",\"COMPONENT_BASE\"],\"title\":\"AdmittanceUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"circuit\":{\"description\":\"The `TransformerCircuit` carrying this transformer's series electrical data.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"magnetizing_shunt\":{\"default\":{\"imag\":0.0,\"real\":0.0},\"description\":\"Magnetizing shunt admittance referenced to the circuit's `base_voltage_primary`. Units: per admittance_units — NATURAL_UNITS: S, COMPONENT_MVAR: MVAr, COMPONENT_BASE: pu .\",\"properties\":{\"imag\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"real\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"title\":\"ComplexNumber\",\"type\":\"object\",\"x-quantity\":\"Susceptance\",\"x-unit-discriminator\":\"admittance_units\",\"x-units\":{\"COMPONENT_BASE\":\"pu\",\"COMPONENT_MVAR\":\"MVAr\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\":\"S\"}},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"shunt_location\":{\"default\":\"PRIMARY\",\"description\":\"Placement of `magnetizing_shunt` on the two sides of the circuit arc.\",\"enum\":[\"PRIMARY\",\"SECONDARY\",\"SPLIT\"],\"title\":\"TwoWindingTransformerShuntLocation\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"circuit\"],\"title\":\"TwoWindingTransformer\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"TwoWindingTransformerShuntLocation\":{\"description\":\"Placement of a `TwoWindingTransformer`'s magnetizing shunt admittance on the two sides of its single circuit arc. PRIMARY: the full magnetizing shunt is applied on the primary (from) side. SECONDARY: the full magnetizing shunt is applied on the secondary (to) side. SPLIT: the full complex magnetizing shunt value is applied on BOTH sides.\",\"enum\":[\"PRIMARY\",\"SECONDARY\",\"SPLIT\"],\"title\":\"TwoWindingTransformerShuntLocation\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"UnitSystem\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis a stored value is expressed in. COMPONENT_BASE: per-unit against a base the component records itself. NATURAL_UNITS: the quantity's own physical unit. No system-wide option: a value per-unitized against a shared base records that base on the component and rides as COMPONENT_BASE. Used in three scopes, each read against its own record rather than a document-wide table: a component's own `power_units` (against that component's `base_power`), a cost payload's own `power_units` (e.g. `CostCurve`, against the owning component's `base_power`), and a time series association's own `unit_system` (governing only that one series).\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"VSCACControlModes\":{\"description\":\"AC-side control mode of a voltage-source-converter (VSC) terminal. AC_REACTIVE_POWER: converter controls reactive power / fixed power factor. AC_VOLTAGE: converter controls the AC-side voltage magnitude.\",\"enum\":[\"AC_REACTIVE_POWER\",\"AC_VOLTAGE\"],\"title\":\"VSCACControlModes\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"VSCDCControlModes\":{\"description\":\"DC-side control mode of a voltage-source-converter (VSC) terminal. DC_POWER: converter controls active power transferred to the DC side. DC_VOLTAGE: converter controls the DC-side voltage. DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP: P-Vdc droop, V_dc = dc_setpoint - droop_gain * P_c.\",\"enum\":[\"DC_POWER\",\"DC_VOLTAGE\",\"DC_VOLTAGE_DROOP\"],\"title\":\"VSCDCControlModes\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"ValueCurve\":{\"description\":\"A cost or fuel curve: function data plus a declaration of how to read its y axis. `INPUT_OUTPUT` reads y as the total `f(x)`, `INCREMENTAL` as the marginal rate `f'(x)`, and `AVERAGE_RATE` as the average `f(x)/x`; the three can express the same underlying function and are inter-convertible given `initial_input`. The `TIME_SERIES_*` variants are the time-varying equivalents. Which form to use follows the data source: bid stacks are incremental, total cost tables input-output, efficiency tables average rate.\",\"discriminator\":{\"mapping\":{\"AVERAGE_RATE\":\"#/components/schemas/AverageRateCurve\",\"INCREMENTAL\":\"#/components/schemas/IncrementalCurve\",\"INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_AVERAGE_RATE\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INCREMENTAL\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\"},\"propertyName\":\"curve_type\"},\"oneOf\":[{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/IncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/AverageRateCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\"}],\"title\":\"ValueCurve\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"VirtualParticipant\":{\"\$schema\":\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\"description\":\"A virtual (convergence) market participant. Supply offers map to the operating cost's incremental offer curves; demand bids map to decremental offer curves. Settles either at a settlement point or at associated trading hubs — the two are mutually exclusive; hub membership is carried as TradingHubAssociation rows rather than a list on this record, matching the trading hub's own membership convention.\",\"properties\":{\"available\":{\"description\":\"Indicator of whether the participant is available for market clearing (`true`) or not (`false`).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"Unique integer identifier for this component.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_demand\":{\"description\":\"Maximum envelope for the decremental (demand) side. Units: MW.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MW\"},\"max_supply\":{\"description\":\"Maximum envelope for the incremental (supply) side. Units: MW.\",\"type\":\"number\",\"x-unit\":\"MW\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Name of the component. Components of the same type (e.g., `PowerLoad`) must have unique names, but components of different types (e.g., `PowerLoad` and `ACBus`) can have the same name.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"operation_cost\":{\"description\":\"Bid curves as an offer-curve operating cost.\",\"discriminator\":{\"mapping\":{\"MARKET_BID\":\"#/components/schemas/MarketBidCost\",\"MARKET_BID_TIME_SERIES\":\"#/components/schemas/MarketBidTimeSeriesCost\"},\"propertyName\":\"cost_type\"},\"oneOf\":[{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/MarketBidCost\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-1068b1dda553e6e25b3b.json#/components/schemas/MarketBidTimeSeriesCost\"}]},\"settlement_point_id\":{\"description\":\"ID of the location this participant settles at — a bus, area, or load zone. `null` when the participant settles at trading hubs instead.\",\"type\":[\"integer\",\"null\"]}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"name\",\"available\",\"max_supply\",\"max_demand\",\"operation_cost\"],\"title\":\"VirtualParticipant\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"VoltageUnitBasis\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis a voltage setpoint is stored in. NATURAL_UNITS: kilovolts. COMPONENT_BASE: per-unit on the component's own base voltage (the connected bus's base voltage for AC setpoints — PSS/E RAW native for FACTS VSET — and the device voltage base PSS/E supplies for DC-line converters and CZ=2 transformer windings). There is no separate system-base option: bus-base per-unit is the device base for voltage.\",\"enum\":[\"NATURAL_UNITS\",\"COMPONENT_BASE\"],\"title\":\"VoltageUnitBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"XY_Coords\":{\"description\":\"A single point, given as its `x` and `y` coordinates.\",\"properties\":{\"x\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"y\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"x\",\"y\"],\"title\":\"XY_Coords\",\"type\":\"object\"}}},\"info\":{\"description\":\"Power system operations models: Topology, Branch, StaticInjection, and Service components\",\"title\":\"PowerOperationsOpenAPIModels\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"},\"openapi\":\"3.1.0\",\"paths\":{}}"),
